      "title": "Setup \u00b7 read before queueing",
      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "# Reference Audition \u00b7 controlled reference comparisons\n\n1. Bake a Flux.2 bundle with 2\u20134 reference images using RefMod_Bake_Image_Families.json and its matching VAE. Choose flux2 BEFORE baking. This graph targets Klein Base 4B with its Qwen3-4B text encoder and Flux.2 VAE.\n2. Choose that saved bundle in Reference Audition. None intentionally stops execution until you choose one. Edit the positive/negative text nodes. Do not apply references upstream.\n3. Queue once. The first row uses every reference; subsequent rows omit one reference each. The seed, prompt, 512\u00d7512 target and sampler settings stay fixed. Flux2Scheduler is connected to sigmas; its steps override Audition's steps, scheduler and denoise widgets. Keep scheduler dimensions matched to the target. The Base preset uses 20 steps and CFG 5; CFG 1 disables classifier-free guidance. Five renders and a 120s soft budget are starting limits. An in-flight render finishes before the time budget is checked; skipped reference numbers appear in the report.\n4. Inspect the contact sheet. Change measures influence, NOT improvement, identity accuracy or quality. For example, compare the baseline against Without reference 2 to see what reference 2 contributes.\n5. Enter references to KEEP in Save Audition Selection, e.g. 1,3. Numbering follows the original bake order. Choose a new name, enable save, then queue again. With ComfyUI's upstream cache retained, only the saver runs. Keep seed fixed. The source bundle is preserved; overwrite is off.\n\n## Other families\n\nThis example is wired for Flux.2. To adapt it, replace the model components AND target latent together. Qwen/Fibo/MOSS/Krea need clip and the Audition prompt widgets; remove the upstream positive/negative connections and enter the prompt inside Audition. Flux uses the wired text conditions. Replace/disconnect Flux2Scheduler when moving to another family. The official MOSS adapter needs Moss-Image-Edit; the official Krea style adapter needs Krea2 style reference. Set CFG, steps and model patches for that family as in its Apply example. MOSS/Krea also need a matching edit LoRA. LTX needs clean video conditioning and a video target; use Euler. Audition fixes target noise and crops guides before decoding. H3 bundles appear as H3: <name> and need H3 prompt conditioning and a plain video target; split nested AV first. Video previews show first/middle/last frames; audio is not auditioned.\n\nUse production checkpoint settings for a final comparison. Low-step trials are for screening; findings can change with the scene and seed."
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "# Reference Audition \u00b7 controlled reference comparisons\n\n1. Bake a Flux.2 bundle with 2\u20134 reference images using RefMod_Bake_Image_Families.json and its matching VAE. Choose flux2 BEFORE baking. This graph targets Klein Base 4B with its Qwen3-4B text encoder and Flux.2 VAE.\n2. Choose that saved bundle in Reference Audition. None intentionally stops execution until you choose one. Edit the positive/negative text nodes. Do not apply references upstream.\n3. Queue once. The first row uses every reference; subsequent rows omit one reference each. The seed, prompt, 512\u00d7512 target and sampler settings stay fixed. Flux2Scheduler is connected to sigmas; its steps override Audition's steps, scheduler and denoise widgets. Keep scheduler dimensions matched to the target. The Base preset uses 20 steps and CFG 5; CFG 1 disables classifier-free guidance. Five renders and a 120s soft budget are starting limits. An in-flight render finishes before the time budget is checked; skipped reference numbers appear in the report.\n4. Inspect the contact sheet. Change measures influence, NOT improvement, identity accuracy or quality. For example, compare the baseline against Without reference 2 to see what reference 2 contributes.\n5. Enter references to KEEP in Save Audition Selection, e.g. 1,3. Numbering follows the original bake order. Choose a new name, enable save, then queue again. With ComfyUI's upstream cache retained, only the saver runs. Keep seed fixed. The source bundle is preserved; overwrite is off.\n\n## Other families\n\nThis example is wired for Flux.2. To adapt it, replace the model components AND target latent together. Qwen/Fibo/MOSS/Krea need clip and the Audition prompt widgets; remove the upstream positive/negative connections and enter the prompt inside Audition. Flux uses the wired text conditions. Replace/disconnect Flux2Scheduler when moving to another family. The official MOSS adapter needs Moss-Image-Edit; the official Krea style adapter needs Krea2 style reference. Set CFG, steps and model patches for that family as in its Apply example. MOSS/Krea also need a matching edit LoRA. LTX needs clean video conditioning and a video target; use Euler. Audition fixes target noise and crops guides before decoding. H3 bundles appear as H3: <name> and need H3 prompt conditioning and a plain video target; split nested AV first. Video previews show first/middle/last frames; audio is not auditioned.\n\nUse production checkpoint settings for a final comparison. Low-step trials are for screening; findings can change with the scene and seed."
      }
    },
